SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE CURSOR RULES

You are working inside a modular Flutter architecture called “Systems”.

Strictly follow these architectural constraints when creating or
modifying any system.

  ---------------------------
  GLOBAL ARCHITECTURE RULES
  ---------------------------

1.  Every system MUST be a separate Flutter package inside: systems//

2.  Each system MUST implement SystemModule.

3.  Each system MUST use GetIt.asNewInstance() for dependency isolation.

4.  Systems MUST depend only on:

    -   core_system
    -   Their own internal files

5.  Direct system-to-system dependency is strictly forbidden.

  -------------------------
  REQUIRED FILE STRUCTURE
  -------------------------

systems// │ ├── lib/ │ ├── core/ │ │ ├── di/ │ │ │ └── _locator.dart │ │
└── module/ │ │ └── _module.dart │ │ │ ├── features/ │ │ └── / │ │ ├──
bloc/ │ │ ├── data/ │ │ ├── domain/ │ │ ├── model/ │ │ ├── view/ │ │ └──
widgets/ │ │ │ ├── shared/ │ │ │ └── _layout.dart │ ├── pubspec.yaml └──
test/

  ------------------------
  SYSTEM MODULE CONTRACT
  ------------------------

Each system MUST implement:

class Module implements SystemModule

Required overrides:

-   String get id
-   String get name
-   ActiveSystemEnum get system
-   List get providers
-   Map<String, RouteFactory> get routes
-   List get homeSections

The constructor MUST call setupLocator().

  ---------------------------
  DEPENDENCY ISOLATION RULE
  ---------------------------

final GetIt Locator = GetIt.asNewInstance();

Never use global GetIt. Never register services outside the system
locator.

  -------------------------
  REGISTRATION FLOW RULES
  -------------------------

1.  Add the system package inside systems/
2.  Add it to root pubspec.yaml dependencies.
3.  Register the module inside:
    lib/app/modules/generated/enabled_modules.dart
4.  Ensure ActiveSystemEnum includes the new system.
5.  Verify routes are exposed via ModulesRegistry.

  ----------------------------------------------
  CI/CD INTEGRATION RULE (Deploy APK Workflow)
  ----------------------------------------------

When adding a new system, you MUST also update:

.github/workflows/deploy_apk.yml

Required updates:

1.  Add a new workflow_dispatch boolean input: enable_

2.  Update ACTIVE_SYSTEMS builder step: Add conditional block to append
    system key.

3.  Update enabled_modules.dart generator case block:

    -   Add import mapping
    -   Add module instantiation mapping

4.  Update DIR_MAP inside “Flutter Test (selected systems)” step:
    [“”]=“”

5.  Update SYSTEM_PACKAGES map in Tree-Shaking Verification step:
    [“”]=“package:”

6.  Ensure tree-shaking validation includes the new system.

Failure to update CI/CD workflow will cause: - System not selectable
during release - Tests not executed - Tree-shaking validation to fail -
Build pipeline inconsistency

  -------------------------------
  MINIMAL EMPTY SYSTEM TEMPLATE
  -------------------------------

pubspec.yaml:

name:

dependencies: flutter: sdk: flutter core_system: path: ../core_system
get_it: any

------------------------------------------------------------------------

_module.dart:

class Module implements SystemModule {

Module() { setupLocator(); }

@override String get id => ‘’;

@override String get name => ‘’;

@override ActiveSystemEnum get system => ActiveSystemEnum.;

@override List get providers => [];

@override Map<String, RouteFactory> get routes => {};

@override List get homeSections => []; }

------------------------------------------------------------------------

_locator.dart:

final GetIt Locator = GetIt.asNewInstance();

void setupLocator() { // Register services here }

  ----------------------
  VALIDATION CHECKLIST
  ----------------------

✔ System folder created ✔ pubspec.yaml configured ✔ Module implements
SystemModule ✔ Locator uses GetIt.asNewInstance() ✔ Enum updated ✔
Module registered in enabled_modules.dart ✔ CI/CD workflow updated ✔ No
cross-system imports

  ------------------------
  ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLE
  ------------------------

The main application must only interact with SystemModule. Feature
details must remain inside the system package.
